{
  "id": "tech-lead-execute-b",
  "name": "Tech-Lead Execute \u2014 plan, execute, verify, close",
  "description": "Wraps the tech-lead card. plan (decompose spec to tasks via to-tickets) \u2192 [dynamic developer cards] \u2192 verify (adversarial-review on integrated work) \u2192 close. Tech-lead card stays intact \u2014 runs loops-engineering internally. Template enforces boundaries.",
  "trigger": {
    "source": "card_completed",
    "condition": {
      "assignee": "tech-lead",
      "status": "done",
      "title_prefix": "[spec]"
    }
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "plan",
      "profile": "tech-lead",
      "skill": "loops-engineering",
      "body_template": "## Implementation Planning\n\n**Spec card:** ${trigger.card_id}\n**Title:** ${trigger.title}\n\nYou are the tech-lead. The PO has already written the spec \u2014 DO NOT grill the user. Your job is implementation planning.\n\n### Phase 1: Discover\n\nRead the spec card body for full requirements. Read the codebase: AGENTS.md, existing tests, conventions, structure. Understand what exists today.\n\n### Phase 2: Plan (autonomous decomposition)\n\nLoad your `to-tickets` skill. Decompose the spec into atomic tasks. For each task:\n- Title (short, actionable)\n- Acceptance criteria (checklist of testable assertions)\n- Dependencies (which tasks must complete before this one)\n- Sizing (small/medium/large)\n\nCreate kanban cards on THIS board for each task:\n- Assign each to `developer`\n- Use parent-children links to enforce dependency ordering\n- Title prefix: `[task]`\n- Body: acceptance criteria + constraints from spec\n\nNO human approval needed. NO beads \u2014 kanban cards only. Fully autonomous.\n\nWrite contract.md to the project workspace with the full task list.\n\n**Completion metadata:**\n```\n{plan_complete: true, task_count: N, task_ids: [\"t_xxx\", ...], sizing_summary: \"small:N medium:N large:N\"}\n```",
      "title_template": "[tl] Plan: ${trigger.title}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "plan_complete",
            "task_count",
            "tasks"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "plan_complete": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "task_count": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "tasks": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "title",
                  "acs",
                  "dependencies",
                  "sizing"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "title": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "acs": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  },
                  "dependencies": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  },
                  "sizing": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "small",
                      "medium",
                      "large"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              },
              "minItems": 1
            },
            "task_ids": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "sizing_summary": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verify",
      "profile": "verifier",
      "skill": "adversarial-review",
      "body_template": "## Overall Verification \u2014 integrated feature\n\n**Spec card:** ${trigger.card_id}\n**Plan:** see plan card ${nodes.plan.output.task_ids} on this board\n\nThis is OVERALL verification \u2014 not per-task. All developer cards are complete and their work is merged. Your job:\n\n1. **Integration check**: do all tasks work TOGETHER? No conflicts, no missing wiring.\n2. **Spec compliance**: does the complete implementation satisfy the ORIGINAL spec from ${trigger.card_id}?\n3. **Acceptance criteria**: verify EVERY AC from the plan against the integrated code.\n4. **Code review**: run adversarial-review on the complete diff (all tasks combined).\n5. **Edge cases**: falsify the integrated feature \u2014 try to break it.\n\nLoad your `adversarial-review` skill.\n\n**Verdict routing:**\n- PASS (zero findings): merge to main, complete with verdict=PASS\n- FAIL: create fix cards for developers, complete with verdict=FAIL\n- ESCALATE (iter >= 3 or spec gap): complete with verdict=ESCALATE\n\n**Completion metadata:**\n```\n{verdict: \"PASS\"|\"FAIL\"|\"ESCALATE\", findings_count: N, acs_verified: N, acs_total: N}\n```",
      "title_template": "[verify] Integration: ${trigger.title}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "verdict"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "PASS",
                "FAIL",
                "ESCALATE"
              ]
            },
            "findings_count": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "acs_verified": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "acs_total": {
              "type": "integer"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": [
        "plan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "close",
      "profile": "tech-lead",
      "skill": "loops-engineering",
      "body_template": "## Close \u2014 wrap up the sprint\n\n**Spec card:** ${trigger.card_id}\n**Verdict:** ${nodes.verify.output.verdict}\n\nAll tasks are complete. The verifier has run overall verification.\n\n### If PASS:\n- Write journal entry (what worked, what didn't)\n- Run reflection (what to learn)\n- Complete this card with verdict=merged\n\n### If ESCALATE:\n- Read the verifier's findings\n- Classify: defect-bug (route to debugger) / contract-gap (re-contract) / harness-ceiling (switch model) / wrong-slice (abandon)\n- Take action based on classification\n- Complete with verdict=escalated\n\n**Completion metadata:**\n```\n{verdict: \"merged\"|\"escalated\", tasks_planned: N, tasks_completed: N, escalate_reason: \"\"}\n```",
      "title_template": "[tl] Close: ${trigger.title}",
      "output": {
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "verdict"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "verdict": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "merged",
                "escalated"
              ]
            },
            "tasks_planned": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "tasks_completed": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "escalate_reason": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "depends_on": [
        "verify"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "from": "plan",
      "to": "verify",
      "condition": "${nodes.plan.output.plan_complete} == True"
    },
    {
      "from": "verify",
      "to": "close"
    }
  ]
}